tes and debate prep  and and there's two real things that you  have to focus on as preparing a  candidate  which number one is prepared for any  question so that you can answer it  answer it and then turn around and pivot  and go back and deliver your message  and the message of of donald trump  and mike pence is that they are the best  to lead  the country economically out of this  crisis  and so you saw the president last night  was able to turn this back around and  make it an economic issue it seems like  it was a crazy way to do it but he was  able to do it  and that is their message and that's  what you're going to expect vice  president pence doing tonight he's going  to  he's going to pilot her attacks i mean  she's a former prosecutor she's going to  be good  you saw what she did to joe biden during  the debates and how she attacked him  ruthlessly and implying that he was a  racist  you know terry's gonna have to turn back  terry we were just looking at some  numbers this morning showing uh  that the trump pence ticket is trailing  among seniors people over the age of 65  by double digits i mean in fact in the  20s and this is a group that  the president won in 2016. a lot of that  has got to do with the virus response do  you expect a different tone  from vice president pence the head of  the coronavirus task force this evening  sure i mean look i think you can expect  the same tone that you have from vice  president  pence all the time but that is a very  different tone than the president's tone  um so i think you're going to expect  more of the same from him from as far as  a tone  but that's always been a very different  tone than the uh than the president's  tone so  you know it will change but but he's  going to be consistent  jamal i know that you have coached  candidates in the past when debating a  woman  i didn't even know that was a thing so  what is the difference on how  on how debate prep is handled when  you're working with a female candidate  question for you both jamal yeah i think  every  yeah everybody has gail everybody has a  couple of different things to worry  about i mean barack obama had to be  worried about being an angry black man  when he was  you know out there doing some of the  debate uh those debates kamala harris  has to be worried about being a black  woman in a very similar  a very similar context um but for mike  pence i think he's got to be worried  about whether or not  he seems too aggressive when he's coming  at kamala harris i mean he can  he can obviously he's got to go at her  record he's got to talk about her and  whether or not  absolutely absolutely but you always  have to calibrate how people are getting  this at home and so you got to pay a  little bit of attention to that  but then we have donald trump on the  other hand who threw all the rules out  the window i mean he  stalked hillary clinton as they walked  around that debate stage four years ago  i mean he but nobody can do what donald  trump can do  uh he's a candidate of his own the  question for for kamala harris is going  to be can she go after donald trump's  record  even though that he's you know obviously  sick but he says he's back in the game  so i think he's fair game for tonight um  with and knowing that mike pence is  going to be a fierce  sometimes monotone but a fierce defender  of their record  even though this trump white house shows  that it can't be trusted  to do the right thing when it comes to  the virus we're all at home right now  because they haven't figured out how to  solve this problem all right terry you  want to wrap it up in 30 seconds  yeah i i think that that we're not all  at home because they haven't figured out  how to solve this problem  i think those are the kind of the over  the top like look we've got a national  crisis  we're trying to get through this there's  plenty of blame to go around but but  it's it's with the coronavirus  not a politician all right terry  sullivan  jamal simmons always good to see you

